// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ⚠️ USING THE "GOD MODE - Quad Consensus" PINE INDICATOR? IGNORE THIS FILE.
//
// That script sends its alerts with Pine's alert() function, which means:
//   1. the alert's Condition MUST be "Any alert() function call", and
//   2. this Message box is IGNORED - TradingView sends the script's own text.
//
// The bridge reads the hidden [[DRFX]] tag inside that text and gets the
// symbol, direction, entry, stop and targets exactly. Nothing to paste.
//
// The templates below are for plain indicators that have no alert() calls of
// their own, where you do type the message yourself.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DrFX GodMode - TradingView alert message templates
//
// Paste ONE of these blocks into the "Message" box of a TradingView alert.
// (This file has comments for your benefit; TradingView's box must contain
// only the JSON itself, with no // lines.)
//
// Webhook URL to use alongside it:
//   https://drfx-godmode-bridge.YOURNAME.workers.dev/tv?key=YOUR_WEBHOOK_KEY
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


// 1. MINIMAL - just symbol and direction
{"symbol":"{{ticker}}","side":"BUY"}


// 2. TYPICAL - an indicator alert with fixed levels
{"symbol":"{{ticker}}","side":"BUY","score":90,"conf":85,
 "tp1":"3378","tp2":"3386","sl":"3362","tf":"{{interval}}"}


// 3. FROM PLOTS - levels come from your Pine script's plot() outputs.
//    {{plot_0}} is the first plot in the script, {{plot_1}} the second, etc.
{"symbol":"{{ticker}}","side":"BUY","score":90,"conf":85,
 "entry":"{{close}}","tp1":"{{plot_0}}","tp2":"{{plot_1}}","sl":"{{plot_2}}",
 "tf":"{{interval}}","note":"GodMode"}


// 4. FROM A STRATEGY - direction follows the strategy's own order
{"symbol":"{{ticker}}","side":"{{strategy.order.action}}","score":88,"conf":80,
 "entry":"{{strategy.order.price}}","tf":"{{interval}}",
 "note":"{{strategy.order.comment}}"}


// 5. CLOSE / FLAT - clears the direction colour on the screen
{"symbol":"{{ticker}}","side":"FLAT","note":"closed"}


// 6. PLAIN TEXT - if JSON is awkward, this is parsed just as well
XAUUSD BUY score=96 conf=94 tp1=3378 tp2=3386 sl=3362


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FIELD REFERENCE
//
//   symbol   text, up to 12 chars   shown large on the card
//   side     BUY | SELL | FLAT      sets the colour and the arrow
//                                   (LONG/SHORT/CLOSE are accepted too)
//   score    0-100                  drives the big ring gauge
//   conf     0-100                  shown as CONF at bottom right
//   entry    text                   currently unused by the display
//   tp1,tp2  text                   shown in green
//   sl       text                   shown in red
//   tf       text, up to 6 chars    timeframe, e.g. 15
//   note     text, up to 24 chars   free text
//
// Anything you leave out simply shows as "-". Field names are flexible:
// "action"/"signal"/"direction" all work for side, "target1"/"tp" for tp1,
// "stop"/"stoploss" for sl, "confidence"/"probability" for conf.
//
// USEFUL TRADINGVIEW PLACEHOLDERS
//   {{ticker}}    {{exchange}}   {{close}}    {{open}}   {{high}}   {{low}}
//   {{volume}}    {{interval}}   {{time}}     {{timenow}}
//   {{plot_0}} ... {{plot_N}}    values of your script's plots
//   {{strategy.order.action}}    buy or sell
//   {{strategy.order.price}}     fill price
//   {{strategy.order.comment}}   your comment text
//   {{strategy.position_size}}   current position size
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
